# Islamic marketing content standards

All reviews, pin drafts, hooks, image text, CTAs, and product marketing copy for this site must stay within Islamically permissible content.

## Do not create or promote

- Non-Islamic religious festival celebration (Christmas, Easter, Halloween, Valentine’s as romance festival, etc.)
- Santa, nativity, worship of other than Allah, religious icons used as celebration marketing
- Alcohol, intoxicants, pork/haram food as a selling angle
- Gambling, interest/riba products, fortune-telling, witchcraft, astrology
- Immodest, sexual, dating, or lingerie marketing
- Music/entertainment that is clearly haram as the product pitch (when avoidable)

## Preferred framing

- Seasonal winter/family DIY, kitchen tools, home convenience, skincare practicality
- Gift occasions: birthdays, housewarming, family gatherings, teacher appreciation, weddings
- Honest product facts without encouraging haram use

## If an Amazon listing is festival-branded

- You may affiliate the useful tool only if our copy reframes to permissible use (e.g. winter baking tools, washable window markers)
- Do not use “celebrate Christmas/Easter/Halloween” hooks, pin text, or CTAs
- Do not spotlight Santa, angels-as-Christmas-symbols, or religious festival rituals in our marketing

## When unsure

Choose the more cautious wording, or skip the product/angle.
